From: CHEN Xuan <chenxuan@iscas.ac.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] device-libs: retain IR names for textual IR tests

The distribution Clang defaults to discarding IR value names. The upstream
atomic fence checks require the entry label. Explicitly retain names for
these tests instead of changing their checks or the compiler implementation.
The reviewed upstream test history has no corresponding harness fix.

--- a/amd/device-libs/test/compile/RunCompileTest.cmake
+++ b/amd/device-libs/test/compile/RunCompileTest.cmake
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 # individual tests.
 
 execute_process(COMMAND
-  ${CLANG_BIN} -O3 -S -cl-std=CL2.0
+  ${CLANG_BIN} -O3 -S -cl-std=CL2.0 -fno-discard-value-names
   -target amdgcn-amd-amdhsa -mcpu=${TEST_CPU}
   -Xclang -finclude-default-header
   --rocm-path=${BINARY_DIR}
